# API of the {{ twin_name }} twin

Root: `${{ '{' }}{{ base_url_env }}}/api/v1`. Every request needs `Authorization: Bearer ${{ '{' }}{{ token_env }}}`, except `GET /healthz` (outside the root), which only says the service is up.

The authoritative description, with every parameter and response schema, is `GET /api/v1/openapi.json`. This file is the short form.

## Parameters many endpoints share

| Parameter | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `at` | version to read: `head` (default), a commit id, `#<n>`, or an ISO 8601 time with an offset |
| `branch` | branch to read; default `main` |
| `format` | `json` (default), `arrow`, `parquet`; or an `Accept` header of `application/vnd.apache.arrow.stream` or `application/vnd.apache.parquet` |
| `limit` | most rows of any table (listings, `/graph/edges`, `/block/*`, versions, logs); JSON default 100 and at most 10,000; Arrow and Parquet return everything unless given |
| `cursor` | `next_cursor` of the previous page |
| `columns`, `properties`, `types`, `edge_types`, `uids` | lists: repeat the parameter or separate values with commas |

Responses that read data name the version they read: `"version": {"id", "seq", "t"}` in JSON; `x-dta-version-id`, `x-dta-version-seq`, `x-dta-version-t` headers on Arrow and Parquet.

## Meta

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /meta/health` | twin id and name, tier, head version, number of versions, fidelity state, manifest revision and hash; `clock` (`kind`, `available`, `now`: the twin's time); `sync` (`interval`, `staleness`, `freshness_s`, `fresh`, `questions`, `sources`, `last_run`, `job`), null for a static twin; `compute` (`worker`: whether the twin has one and whether it answers; `questions`: how many are validated, provisional and failing; `job`: the compute job in progress) |
| `GET /meta/schema?at=` | object and link types with ancestors, link ends and properties (kind, unit, required, role, description); abstract classes with their concrete kinds; enums |
| `GET /meta/schema/linkml?at=` | the same schema as LinkML text |
| `GET /meta/manifest?at=` | the twin's manifest: contract, sources (without secrets), mappings |

## Objects

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /objects/{type}?columns=&where=&sort=&count=&include=provenance` | objects of a type (or of an abstract class), paged in uid order, or in the order of `sort` (`<property>`, or `-<property>` for descending; objects without a value last) |
| `GET /objects?uid_like=&types=&include_meta=&count=` | `uid` and `type` of every object, of any type, whose uid matches an SQL pattern (`%` any run of characters, `_` one), in uid order; the twin's own record types are left out unless `types` names them or `include_meta=true` |
| `GET /objects/{type}/{uid}?include=provenance` | one object |
| `GET /object/{uid}` | one object, whatever its type |
| `GET /search?q=&types=&include_meta=&count=` | `uid`, `type` and `name` of every object, of any type, whose uid or whose name matches an SQL pattern, in uid order; one request instead of one per type |
| `GET /objects/{type}/{uid}/links?direction=out\|in\|both&edge_types=&edge_where=` | the object's edges and what is at their other end |
| `GET /objects/{type}/{uid}/history?range=&properties=` | one row per version in which the object changed |

`where` is repeated: `<property>:<op>:<value>` with `eq ne lt le gt ge in like null notnull`.

`count=true` adds the number of rows of the whole listing, all pages: `total` in JSON, the header `x-dta-total` in every format.

## Graph

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /graph/neighbors?seed=&depth=&direction=&edge_types=&edge_where=&limit=` | nodes within `depth` hops of the seeds, with type and depth, and the edges between them |
| `GET /graph/paths?source=&target=&max_depth=&k=&weight=&direction=&edge_types=&edge_where=` | up to `k` simple paths of at most `max_depth` hops (default 6, at most 64), shortest first; each path has `nodes`, `edges` (each with `src`, `dst`, `edge_type`, `link_uid`), `hops` and `cost` |
| `POST /graph/subgraph` body `{seeds, depth, direction, edge_types, edge_where, node_types, limit, properties}`; `part=nodes\|edges` picks the table for Arrow and Parquet | the part of the graph reached from the seeds |
| `GET /graph/edges?edge_types=&edge_where=` | every edge: `src`, `dst`, `edge_type`, `link_uid` |

`edge_where` is repeated: `<LinkType>.<property>:<op>:<value>`, with the operators of `where`. A link of that type is followed, and returned, only when it passes; the name may be an abstract class, which stands for every link type under it. Links of types the filter does not name, and references, are not affected: combine it with `edge_types` to follow nothing else.

## History

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /history/versions?from=&to=&cause=&actor=&run=&backfill=&order=asc\|desc` | versions with their time, cause, actor and note |
| `GET /history/versions/{selector}` | the one version a selector names |
| `GET /history/diff?from=&to=&types=&detail=summary\|rows` | rows added, modified and removed per type, or the rows themselves |
| `GET /history/branches` | branches and their heads |

## Block (whole tables)

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /block/nodes/{type}?columns=` | every object of a type at a version |
| `GET /block/edges/{edge_type}` | every edge of one type, with the link's properties |
| `GET /block/slice/{type}?range=&properties=&uids=&mode=state\|changes&layout=long\|tensor` | the type's objects over a range of versions |
| `POST /block/training-set` body `{target, uids, start, end, branch, step, features, ahead, horizon}` | a frame for learning: one row per object and grid time (`unique_id`, `ds`, `y`, a column per feature and, with `horizon`, `label` and `label_ds`), every value the one stored at or before its time; `meta` (schema metadata `dta:training` in Arrow and Parquet) says what the rows hold |

As JSON these are paged like every other table; as Arrow or Parquet they come whole.

## Sync

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /sync/sources` | per source: `status` (`ok`, `failing`, `disabled`), `last_error`, `watermark` (the time of its newest data), `last_success_at`, `freshness_s`, its `datasets` with how far each has been read, its `mappings`; and the twin's `clock` |
| `GET /sync/runs?status=&kind=` | the runs that loaded or synced the twin, newest first: `status` (`running`, `succeeded`, `partial`, `failed`), `kind` (`backfill`, `incremental`, `replay`), when it started and finished, versions and rows written, rows set aside and late, `error` |
| `GET /sync/runs/{uid}` | one run |
| `GET /sync/runs/{uid}/rejects?rule=&mapping=` | the rows the run set aside (which row, which rule it broke and why; never the row's values); `total` counts the rows that pass the filters; a cursor is refused once the file has changed: start again |
{% if live %}
| `POST /sync/runs`, body `{}`, `{"sources": [...]}` or `{"replay": {"source": ..., "dataset": ...}}`, optional header `Idempotency-Key` | starts a run now and answers `{"job": {...}}`: 202 for a new job, 200 when the same run is already queued or running |
{% endif %}

## Lifecycle

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /lifecycle/jobs?kind=&state=&lane=` | work the API does in the background, newest first: `id`, `kind`, `lane` (`sync` for sync runs, `compute` for other long work; the jobs of a lane run one at a time, in order), `state` (`queued`, `running`, `succeeded`, `failed`), `result`, `error`, `trace_id`, `duration_ms` |
| `GET /lifecycle/jobs/{id}` | one job, as `{"data": {...}}` |
| `GET /lifecycle/logs?level=&since=&context=&trace_id=&service=&limit=` | the twin's own structured log lines, newest first |
| `GET /lifecycle/schedule` | what the twin's scheduler asks for and when: `now` on the twin's clock and `entries`, each `{id, kind, interval, method, path, key, body}`: the sync run, the fidelity check, the reconciliation of executed actions (when the twin can execute one), each enabled control loop and each function triggered on an interval; empty for a static twin |
| `GET /lifecycle/notifications` | the last 200 notifications the twin sent since it started, newest first, each with its `status` (`queued`, `delivered`, `failed`, `dropped`, `logged`, `unsent`), `tries` and `http_status`; the address they go to is never shown |
| `POST /lifecycle/register` body `{"code": <sha256>\|null}` | brings the twin's functions, models, questions, action types and control loops in line with its manifest in one version, and none when nothing differs: `functions`, `models` and `questions`, each with what was `created`, `changed` and left `unchanged`; `actions` and `loops`, each also with what was `orphaned` (no longer declared: disabled); and the `version`. A new loop is disabled until it is enabled. `code` is the hash `POST /artifacts` gave for the twin's packed code |

