## Fidelity

Whether the twin still keeps what it promised, measured on its own clock at every fidelity interval. States: `unknown` (no check yet), `healthy`, `correcting` (something is being put right), `failed` (the twin could not put itself right).

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /fidelity` | `state`, `since`, the last `check`, per question the origin scored, its error, the error over the window against the tolerance and whether it is in breach, the incidents not resolved, the suspect signals |
| `POST /fidelity/checks`, optional header `Idempotency-Key` | a check of the newest boundary of the fidelity interval, as a job of the compute lane; a boundary already checked answers from its record |
| `GET /fidelity/checks?from=&to=&limit=&cursor=` | the checks, newest first |
| `GET /fidelity/checks/{uid}` | one check: what was measured per question, the freshness, the signals tested |
| `GET /fidelity/questions/{id}/errors?from=&to=&format=` | the error of a question per scored origin: `origin`, `scored_at`, `error`, `n`, `model`, `in_window`, `check` |
| `GET /fidelity/incidents?status=&kind=&subject=` | incidents, newest first (`kind`: `breach`, `stale`, `signal`, `reconcile`; `status`: `open`, `remodel_requested`, `failed`, `resolved`) |
| `GET /fidelity/incidents/{id}` | one incident with every step taken |
| `POST /fidelity/incidents/{id}/retry` body `{"by", "note"}` | starts a failed incident's corrections again from the first rung |
| `POST /fidelity/incidents/{id}/resolve` body `{"by", "note"}` | resolves an incident of kind `signal` or `reconcile` by hand |
| `POST /fidelity/corrections` body `{"question", "rung"}` (`recalibrate` or `reselect`) | one correction by hand, as a job: the question's models are evaluated again on recent data |
| `GET /fidelity/signals?status=` | the observed signals found suspect (`stuck` or `biased`), each with the raw `reading` that is kept and not written to the object |
| `POST /fidelity/signals/{uid}/clear` body `{"by", "note"}` | takes a signal off the suspect list; its readings are written again |

## Actions

What the twin may do to the real system, and what became of each proposal. An action type carries out a control (`autonomy`: `advisory` is a recommendation only, `supervised` waits for an approval, `autonomous` is executed at once) or only advises. The interlock: an autonomous action is executed at once only while the twin's fidelity is `healthy`, or `correcting` with no `stale` or `reconcile` incident unresolved; it is `blocked` while the twin is `unknown` or `failed` or such an incident is open, and its `reasons` name the state or each incident's kind and uid. An approval is blocked only while the twin is `failed`. Every proposal is recorded, whatever became of it.

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /actions?at=` | the action types: `control`, `target`, `object_type`, `binding` (`executor` or `advisory`), `autonomy`, `parameters`, `bounds` (`minimum`, `maximum`, `allowed`, `max_step`), `settle`, `tolerance`, `executable`, `on_failure` (what the control sends when the twin fails: `mode`, `action`, `parameters`, `after_stale`); and `executor_configured` |
| `GET /actions/{id}?at=` | one action type |
| `POST /actions/{id}/propose` body `{"object", "params", "reason", "source"}`, optional header `Idempotency-Key` | judges the proposal at the head and records it: `201` with the record (`200` with the record the key made before); `status` is `proposed` (waiting for an approval, or advice only), `executed`, `failed` or `blocked`. An execution is one HTTP call made inside the request (up to 30 s and two retries of a connection). A refusal is `422` with every reason in `errors` and the record's uid in `record` |
| `GET /actions/records?status=&action=&object=&source=&origin=&reconciliation=&limit=&cursor=` | the records, newest proposal first; `origin` is `failsafe` (sent by a control's `on_failure`, source `failsafe:<control>`), `loop` or `proposal` |
| `GET /actions/records/{uid}` | one record: what was proposed and judged, the decision, the call and its answer, and whether its effect was observed (`reconciliation`: `pending`, `ok`, `mismatch`) |
| `POST /actions/records/{uid}/approve` body `{"by", "note"}` | approves a proposed supervised action and executes it; `blocked` while the twin's fidelity is `failed` |
| `POST /actions/records/{uid}/reject` body `{"by", "note"}` | turns a proposed action down |
| `POST /actions/reconcile`, optional header `Idempotency-Key` | compares every executed action whose `settle` has passed with the observed value: `ok` within `tolerance`, otherwise `mismatch`, which opens an incident of kind `reconcile` (the twin is then `correcting`, and autonomous actions are blocked until it is resolved); an `ok` closes the open incident of an earlier action on the same control and object |

## Control loops

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /control/loops?at=` | the loops: `controls`, `policy` (a function), `interval`, `enabled`, `last_run` |
| `GET /control/loops/{id}?at=` | one loop and what its last run did |
| `POST /control/loops/{id}/enable` body `{"by"}` | lets the loop run; the scheduler asks for it once per interval |
| `POST /control/loops/{id}/disable` body `{"by"}` | stops the loop |
| `POST /control/loops/{id}/run`, optional header `Idempotency-Key` | a run now, as a job of the compute lane (kind `loop`): the policy is asked, and each action it names is proposed as any other, with the loop as its source; the job's result is the run |
{% endif %}

## Functions

What the twin computes: shipped built-ins with the arguments their registration fixes, and code the twin brought, which runs in the twin's worker.

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /functions` | every function: `id`, `kind` (`builtin`, `registered`), `entry`, the fixed `params`, `latency_budget_ms`, `origin` (`manifest`, `runtime`), `status` (`active`, `disabled`) |
| `GET /functions/{id}` | one function, with `parameters`: what its entry takes and which of them are fixed |
| `POST /functions/{id}/run?at=&branch=` body: the arguments by name (a built-in's may be given in the query string instead) | the answer: `value` (a JSON value, or the rows of a table, paged; Arrow and Parquet as elsewhere), `unit`, `interval`, `notes`, the `version` read, `function`, `model`, `provisional` and `reasons`. The function is the one registered now; `at` chooses the data it reads. A function that gives rows to write names the version it wrote in `wrote`; any other run writes nothing. With the header `Idempotency-Key` the run is a job of the compute lane (`202` with `job`, `200` with the job the key made before); its result is the answer, a table as its rows. A function triggered `on_commit` runs after every sync run that wrote; one triggered on an `interval` is asked for by the scheduler; each such run leaves a `TwinFunctionRun` |
| `POST /functions` body `{id, entry, params, description, latency_budget, env, artifact}` | registers a function while the twin runs: 201 with the function |
| `DELETE /functions/{id}` | disables a function registered while the twin ran |

## Questions

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /questions?status=` | every question with what it may claim: `status` (`validated`, `provisional`, `failing`), `reason`, `metric`, `measured_error`, `tolerance`, `unit`, `basis` (`backtest`, `noise_floor`, `latency`), its `function` and active `model` |
| `GET /questions/{id}` | one question |
| `POST /questions/{id}/answer?at=&branch=` body: arguments of its function | the answer of the question's function, as `POST /functions/{id}/run` gives it; `provisional` with `reasons` while the question is not validated, the note `question_failing` when it was measured outside its tolerance |
| `POST /questions/measure` body `{"questions": [...]}` or `{}`, optional header `Idempotency-Key` | starts a job that measures the questions against their tolerances and records what each may claim; answers `{"job": {...}}`, 202 for a new job, 200 when it exists |

## Models

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /models?spec=&status=&question=` | every candidate of every model specification: `uid` (`twin_model:<spec>/<candidate>`), `family`, `params`, `target`, `features`, `status` (`candidate`, `active`, `rejected`, `retired`), what it was fitted on |
| `GET /models/{uid}` | one model, with `state`: the header of its fitted state (range and series fitted, validity, library versions) |
| `GET /models/{uid}/backtests` | its evaluations, newest first: range, origins, horizon, error and the baseline's, every score, whether it was accepted |
| `POST /models/evaluate` body `{"spec": ..., "budget_s": ...}` or `{}`, optional header `Idempotency-Key` | starts a job that backtests every candidate, makes the best accepted one `active` with a fitted state and records the question's status, in one version; answers `{"job": {...}}`, 202 or 200 |
| `POST /models/{uid}/predict?at=&branch=` body `{horizon, levels, interventions}` | `unique_id`, `ds`, `mean` and `lo_<level>`, `hi_<level>` per level, for `horizon` steps after the version; `notes` (`outside_validity`, `no_intervals`) |
| `POST /models` body `{spec, candidate, family \| artifact + entry, params, target, features, question, interventional}` | registers a candidate while the twin runs: 201 with the model |
| `DELETE /models/{uid}` | retires a model registered while the twin ran |

## Scenarios

What the twin would be under assumed changes, each on a branch of its own.

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /scenarios?include_deleted=` | every scenario: `id`, `name`, `branch`, `base_version`, `base_t`, `interventions`, `horizon`, `step`, `models`, `status` (`created`, `running`, `done`, `failed`, `deleted`) |
| `GET /scenarios/{id}` | one scenario, with whether its branch `exists` and where the branch's `head` is |
| `POST /scenarios?at=` body `{name, description, interventions: [{target, uid, value, start, end}], horizon, models}` | makes a scenario from a version of `main`: 201, or 200 with `created: false` when the same request at the same base was made before |
| `POST /scenarios/{id}/run` body `{"budget_s": ...}` or `{}`, optional header `Idempotency-Key` | starts a job in which each model predicts the horizon and the branch gains one version per grid time; answers `{"job": {...}}`, 202 or 200 |
| `GET /scenarios/{id}/compare?targets=&against=&uids=` | `target`, `uid`, `t`, `scenario`, `against`, `difference` on the scenario's grid; `against` is `main` or another scenario of the same base |
| `DELETE /scenarios/{id}` | removes the scenario's branch and marks its record `deleted` |

A scenario's branch is read like any other: pass `branch=<its branch>` to the endpoints above.

## Derived data

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `POST /derived` body `{branch, type, rows, kind, source, inputs_version, confidence, t_valid}` | writes rows that were worked out (`kind`: `inferred`, `assumed`, `simulated`) as one version, each value carrying its `source` (the uid of a function or model) and the version of its inputs: 201 with `{"version", "rows"}`. Observed facts, assumed or simulated facts on `main`, and properties a source fills are refused. At most 100,000 rows and 16 MiB |

## Artifacts

Files kept outside the graph, named by the SHA-256 of their content: code, fitted models, large tables.

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `POST /artifacts` | keeps the request body (any bytes, at most 512 MiB) and answers `{"sha256", "size_bytes", "location"}`: 201 when new, 200 when the same content was already kept. Nothing is written to the graph |
| `GET /artifacts/{sha256}` | the file's bytes; 404 `artifact.not_found` when none is kept under that hash |

## What changes the twin

Each of these writes a new version on `main`, or on a scenario's branch:

- registrations: `POST /lifecycle/register` (no version when nothing differs), `POST /functions`, `DELETE /functions/{id}`, `POST /models`, `DELETE /models/{uid}`;
- evaluations and measurements: `POST /models/evaluate` records the backtests, the active model and its question's status; `POST /questions/measure` records what each question may claim;
- scenarios: `POST /scenarios` and `DELETE /scenarios/{id}` record the scenario on `main`; `POST /scenarios/{id}/run` writes the predictions on the scenario's branch and the run's status on `main`;
- derived data: `POST /derived`;
- running a function that gives rows to write, through `POST /functions/{id}/run`: the answer names the version written in `wrote`;
- runs of functions triggered `on_commit` or on an `interval`, each recorded in a `TwinFunctionRun`;
{% if live %}
- fidelity: every check records what it measured and the twin's state; corrections record their evaluations and the model they make active; `POST /fidelity/incidents/{id}/retry`, `.../resolve` and `POST /fidelity/signals/{uid}/clear` record the step and who took it;
- actions:`POST /actions/{id}/propose`, `POST /actions/records/{uid}/approve`, `.../reject` and `POST /actions/reconcile` record what was decided, sent and observed; `POST /control/loops/{id}/enable`, `.../disable` and `.../run` record the loop's state and its runs. An executed action changes the real system, not the twin's observed data: that changes when a sync run reads it;
- sync runs: `POST /sync/runs` makes the twin read its sources, which is the only way new observed data arrives.
{% endif %}

These never change it: every `GET`; answering a question (`POST /questions/{id}/answer`: rows its function would write are not written); running a function that gives no rows to write; predicting (`POST /models/{uid}/predict`); `POST /graph/subgraph`; `POST /block/training-set`. `POST /artifacts` keeps a file and writes nothing to the graph.

There is no endpoint that edits observed data: {% if live %}it changes only when the sources do and a sync run reads them{% else %}a static twin's data was loaded once and does not change{% endif %}.

Jobs are kept in the API's memory and are forgotten when it restarts. The lasting record of a sync run is in `/sync/runs`, of an evaluation in `/models/{uid}/backtests` and `/questions`, of a scenario in `/scenarios`.
